      "title": "Delaunay triangulation + Voronoi cells",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "cv2.Subdiv2D - Delaunay triangulation and its dual Voronoi diagram - is a stateful class (insert points, then query) rather than a plain function. 'CV Delaunay / Voronoi' inserts, queries and drops it in one run, so no live handle crosses the graph.\n\nThe points here are GFTT corners, but any Nx2 set works: blob centres, k-means centroids, annotated points, tracked features.\n\nDelaunay maximises the smallest angle, so the triangles are as well-shaped as the points allow - that is why it is THE mesh for piecewise-affine image morphing (triangulate landmarks, warp each triangle) and for surface reconstruction from sparse points.\n\nThe Voronoi cell of a point is everything closer to it than to any other point. The cells on the hull are unbounded, so the node clips every one against the enclosing rectangle - connect 'bounds' to the image and they tile it exactly.\n\nTry: raise min_distance on the detector to thin the points out and watch both structures get coarser; the 'edges' output draws the mesh once per edge instead of three times per triangle."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
